.TH AVR\-ORG\-GOVERNANCE 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-org-governance \- Show what you may manage in the organization.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr org governance
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show what you may manage in the organization.
.PP
Shows whether groups, resource access and delegation are on, which organization capabilities you hold, and for each group listed for you what you may and may not do there.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr org governance
    avr org governance --json groups --jq '.groups[].display_name'
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    delegation_enabled, eligible_root_admin, groups, groups_enabled,
    manual_root_capabilities, resource_access_enabled, root_capabilities
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-org (1),
